<https://w3id.org/rete/datacite#> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/license> <https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/> .
<https://w3id.org/rete/datacite#> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "DataCite Ontology (rete)"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rete/datacite#> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Ontology> .
<https://w3id.org/rete/datacite#> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A domain ontology for the DataCite Public Data Files: DOI-identified\n        research outputs (datasets, software, text, images, physical objects, …), their\n        creators, funders and identifiers, and — crucially — the rich relation network\n        between them (Cites, IsSupplementTo, IsVersionOf, IsPartOf, IsDerivedFrom,\n        IsIdenticalTo, …) that also forms the standalone 'PID Links' edge tables.\n\n        Designed for interoperability: research outputs align to schema.org, DCAT and\n        FaBiO; the relation vocabulary aligns to CiTO (citations), Dublin Core and PAV\n        (versioning) and PROV-O (derivation); identifiers to the SPAR DataCite ontology;\n        funding to FRAPO; agents to FOAF/PRO. The PID Links event is reified as a\n        provenance-bearing dcite:PidRelation.\n\n        Kept within OWL 2 QL (domain/range, subClass/subProperty, inverseOf and\n        existential superclass restrictions only — no functional/transitive/cardinality\n        axioms, no property chains) so rete's lazy query-rewriting reasoner can use it."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rete/datacite#> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso> <https://schema.datacite.org/> .
<https://w3id.org/rete/datacite#> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#versionInfo> "1.2.0 (2026-10-19): dcite:FundingReference (hasFundingReference, funder, funderName) and dcite:creatorName / affiliationName / rorId on dcite:AgentRole, so names stay with the record that states them; one dcite:PidRelation per PID Links event (uuid). 1.1.0 (2026-10-16): full DataCite 4.6 relationType and resourceTypeGeneral vocabularies, dcite:fromSnapshot, raw-value properties" .
<https://w3id.org/rete/datacite#Agent> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/rete/datacite#Agent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A creator or contributor of a resource (person or organization), often carrying an ORCID or ROR identifier."@en .
